  "scope": "Three alternating CPU-pinned baseline/candidate pairs cover fourteen preserved completed workflows: eight retained revolution groups, three similarity/native-solid groups, the original clipped-cap extrusion and both original procedural solid revolution/replay recipes. Six absolute processes (three per cohort) cover three newly completed coaxial Boolean/replay workflows, both archive limit/forgery/nesting groups and eight owner point-definition groups. Every process records first invocation and three repeated fresh-input invocations, except the expensive overlapping union/XOR group has one repeated invocation per process. All three processes and complete unchanged geometry remain measured. Assertions and output materialization remain inside timing. Earlier cases can warm immutable global caches; there is no disabled/evicted-cache claim. These instrumented shared-host samples establish neither a general speedup nor internal work/heap/cancellation bounds. Peak process RSS and requested allocation traffic are different quantities. The allocation counter covers Rust GlobalAlloc calls, not foreign allocator internals."
